course: dictionary
lesson: 4603
title: Herring: a fish, a food or a false clue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Context tells you which one. «A shoal of herring swam past the boat.» A shoal is a big group of fish, so here herring is the small silver fish.
explain: «The pickled herring was served on bread at the market.» Here herring is food. Pickled tells you it was preserved and eaten, not swimming in the sea.
explain: Now read this: «Answering a different question to dodge the real one is called a red herring.» There is no fish here at all. A red herring is a clue or fact that leads you the wrong way. Always check: does the meaning fit the sentence?
fact: A herring is a small silver fish that lives in big groups in the North Atlantic and other cold seas.
fact: Herring is also the fish we eat, often smoked as a kipper or pickled.
fact: A red herring is a clue or fact that leads you the wrong way, on purpose or by accident.
fact: The plural can be herring or herrings: one herring, many herrings or a shoal of herring.
fact: «Packed like herrings» means crowded very close together.
exercise: «A shoal of herring swam past the boat.» What is a herring here? | A kind of boat | A large sandy beach | A red clue that leads you the wrong way | *A small silver fish
exercise: Ben says the number 12 in the maths problem is a red herring. What does red herring mean? | *A clue or number that leads you the wrong way | A sum you cannot finish | A number that is very large | A red fish caught in the sea
exercise: «The pickled herring was served on bread at the market.» What does pickled herring mean? | A silver fish that lives in cold rivers | A herring sold without its head | *Herring preserved in a salty or sour liquid and eaten as food | A fish with red spots that swims alone
test: In the phrase «herring gulls», what does herring tell you? | A gull that is silver | A gull that is very old | A gull that eats only fish | *The kind of gull
test: What does the word shoal mean in «a shoal of herring»? | *A large group of fish swimming together | A kind of boat | A type of cold weather | A sandy beach
exam: «The clue was a red herring, so the detective went the wrong way.» What does red herring mean? | A tasty food from the market | A large meal of fish | A red fish caught in the sea | *A false clue that leads you the wrong way
